[2m› To the camp at Millholm[0m[39m[49m

[1mthe camp at Millholm[0m[39m[49m
Millholm is half houses and half wagons with their wheels taken off, painted saf
fron and rose and a deep blue. Cook-smoke drifts between them, smelling of cumin
 and charred onion.
Your brother is sitting on a rail with your father’s old spear across his knees,
 watching the road. He is taller by a head than when you went away.
The grey dog barks twice, for form’s sake, then comes to see who you are.

